      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Han Yangling: The Quieter Emperor’s Tomb", "item": "https://xi-an-china.com/attractions/han-yangling/" }
    ]},
    { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Han Yangling worth visiting if I’ve seen the Terracotta Warriors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Absolutely. It is a completely different experience — miniature figurines instead of life-sized, glass-floored pits instead of open hangars, and peaceful solitude instead of crowds. Many visitors prefer the intimate atmosphere here."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get to Han Yangling?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Taxi from downtown: 40 min, $12-$15. Metro Line 2 to Shitushuguan Station, then bus or taxi (10-15 min). It is less convenient than the Warriors but the solitude is the reward."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is it different from the Terracotta Warriors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Size: 60 cm figures vs. life-sized. Era: Han Dynasty (202 BC) vs. Qin (210 BC). Crowds: dozens per day vs. thousands. Experience: quiet and contemplative vs. bustling and spectacular. They complement rather than compete with each other."}},] }
