        </a>
        <a href="/day-trips" class="group rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 hover:border-terracotta-200 transition-colors no-underline">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-stone-800 group-hover:text-terracotta-700 transition-colors">Day Trips from Xi'an</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-0.5">Where Han Yangling fits in your itinerary.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
<section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-6">FAQ</h2>
      <FaqAccordion items={faqs} />
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/attractions/tang-paradise" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-terracotta-500 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:bg-terracotta-600 active:scale-[0.98]">
        Next: Tang Paradise <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
<section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">The Glass Floor Experience: Walking Above History</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Han Yangling's signature feature is its <strong class="text-stone-800">glass-floored corridors</strong> suspended directly above the excavation pits. Unlike the Terracotta Warriors — where you view from elevated walkways 5-10 meters away — here you stand on transparent panels looking straight down at artifacts exactly where they were buried 2,100 years ago.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Below your feet: rows of miniature terracotta soldiers (about 60 cm tall, compared to life-size at the Warriors), ceramic animals (pigs, dogs, sheep, goats — a full Han Dynasty farm), chariots, and storage jars. The figures are smaller but <strong class="text-stone-800">far more detailed</strong> than the Terracotta Warriors — you can see individual facial expressions, clothing folds, and even traces of the original paint. The museum also displays the tomb of Empress Wang, with jade burial suits and gold ornaments.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-stone-500">Unlike the Warriors, photography is allowed throughout Han Yangling. The low light levels under the glass floor make for atmospheric, museum-quality shots. Bring a fast lens (f/2.8 or wider) if you want crisp photos.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>